  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The point $(5,-5)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $2,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $2.$ What is the resulting point?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,2y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(2x,2y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(5,-5)↦(2\\cdot 5,\\,2\\cdot (-5))=(10,-10).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/8e3eccf9b9190db3c19e2d49d633763d420947daa12929a8516fcf066465165d.png)",
